# ============================================================================
# STIR/SHAKEN x5u endpoint — environment (docker-compose.x5u.yml)
# ============================================================================
# Copy to the repo-root .env used by the compose command, OR export these two
# vars in the shell before `docker compose -f docker-compose.x5u.yml up -d`:
#
#     cp infra/stir/.env.x5u.example .env      # then edit X5U_ACME_EMAIL
#
# Only these TWO variables drive the x5u service. Everything else is fixed in
# docker-compose.x5u.yml / infra/stir/Caddyfile.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Public hostname to serve the cert on AND obtain the Let's Encrypt cert for.
# Must resolve (A record) to the services VM's public IP (see DNS prereq below).
X5U_DOMAIN=certs.granitevoip.com

# ACME contact email — Let's Encrypt sends expiry/issue notices here.
# CHANGE THIS to a monitored ops mailbox before deploying (the default is a
# non-routable placeholder).
X5U_ACME_EMAIL=admin@example.com

# ============================================================================
# DEPLOY (on the East services VM, repo at /opt/revup)
# ============================================================================
#   docker compose -f docker-compose.x5u.yml up -d
#
# Verify once it's up (cert issuance takes a few seconds after DNS is live):
#   curl -sI https://certs.granitevoip.com/stir/8052-2026.pem
#     -> HTTP/2 200
#     -> content-type: application/pem-certificate-chain
#     -> cache-control: public, max-age=86400
#   curl -s  https://certs.granitevoip.com/stir/8052-2026.pem | openssl x509 -noout -subject
#     -> subject=... CN=SHAKEN 8052
#   curl -sI https://certs.granitevoip.com/anything-else   -> HTTP/2 404
#   curl -s  http://127.0.0.1/healthz                      -> ok   (uptime probe)
#
# The final x5u URL (put this in STIR_CERT_URL for the SBCs):
#   https://certs.granitevoip.com/stir/8052-2026.pem

# ============================================================================
# PREREQUISITES (operator, on GCP — NOT performed by this repo)
# ============================================================================
# 1. DNS
#      certs.granitevoip.com   A   34.26.57.37        (the services VM public IP)
#    Required BEFORE first start so the Let's Encrypt HTTP-01 challenge can
#    validate the hostname.
#
# 2. FIREWALL (GCP VPC ingress to the services VM)
#      allow  tcp:80    from 0.0.0.0/0    # ACME HTTP-01 challenge + HTTP->HTTPS
#      allow  tcp:443   from 0.0.0.0/0    # the HTTPS cert endpoint
#    No other new ports. (The main services stack already uses 8080/8443/8088/
#    9060/etc.; those are unchanged.)
#
# 3. CERT FILE (already in the repo — nothing to do)
#      infra/stir/granite-shaken-8052-x5u.pem   = leaf (CN=SHAKEN 8052) +
#      Neustar SHAKEN CA-2 intermediate. PUBLIC, no private key. Served verbatim.

# ============================================================================
# ROTATION (yearly STI-cert renewal)
# ============================================================================
# 1. Drop the new chain PEM (leaf + intermediate, NO key) into infra/stir/.
# 2. Add a handle block in infra/stir/Caddyfile that serves it at a NEW path,
#    e.g. /stir/8052-2027.pem (keep the old path live during cutover so
#    in-flight PASSporTs still verify), then `docker compose -f
#    docker-compose.x5u.yml up -d` to reload.
# 3. Update STIR_CERT_URL in the SBCs' .env to the new URL and redeploy the SBCs
#    (docker-compose.sbc.yml). Retire the old path after the old cert's notAfter.
